# BGCLASS: player classes for Begotten.
#
# Every "class" line starts a class; the lines below it set its numbers.  The
# built-in text of the engine is identical to this file; a BGCLASS lump in your
# own WAD is read afterwards, so it can change a class (repeat its "class"
# line, then list the numbers again -- anything you leave out goes back to the
# default of a new class) or add new ones (up to 8 in total, the first
# three are what class-flagged map things refer to: class 1 = first class,
# class 2 = second class, class 3 = third class).
#
#   class <word> "<Display name>"
#   health <n>                     starting health
#   armor <n>                      starting armor points (green armor when > 0)
#   speed <pct>                    walking / running speed in percent of the original game's (soldier 90, witch 110, swordsman 120)
#   jump <height>                  how high the class' jump rises, in map units (0 = the class cannot jump).
#                                  Soldier 28 (half the player's height), witch 37 (two thirds), swordsman 56
#                                  (its full height).  A ledge can be jumped onto when it is lower than this
#                                  (stairs up to 24 are walked anyway).  Gravity of the sector still applies:
#                                  low-gravity sectors give higher jumps.  The jump button is the JUMP key
#                                  (Right Alt by default) / controller button B.  A map can forbid jumping
#                                  in its UMAPINFO.
#   meleeonly                      the class uses the knife only: it never owns guns and cannot pick up
#                                  weapons or ammunition
#   blade <min> <max>              damage range of the knife (stock punch is 2-20; berserk does not
#                                  apply).  145-205 kills a 150 hp demon in one hit most of the time
#   foeaim <pct>                   how scattered monsters' hitscan fire (zombieman, shotgunner, chaingunner,
#                                  SS, spider mastermind ...) is when aimed at this class, in percent of
#                                  the normal spread: 100 = normal, 0 = every shot aimed dead on
#   parry <tics>                   the class can parry: its secondary fire on the knife raises a guard
#                                  that lasts this many tics (35 per second), see below
#   maxhealth <n>                  health limit of stimpaks, medikits and berserk (normally 100)
#   maxbonus <n>                   limit of health bonuses / potions (normally 200)
#   maxsoul <n>                    limit of the soulsphere (normally 200)
#   megahealth <n>                 what the megasphere sets health to (normally 200)
#                                  (leave a limit out to keep the normal value)
#   weapons <mode> ...             weapons owned at the start (see BGWEAPON for names)
#   ammo <type> <n>                starting ammo (bullets shells belts fire tempest spirit hellfire)
#   maxammo <type> <pct>           ammo capacity in percent of the normal maximum
#   swapspeed <category> <pct>    how fast the class raises / lowers weapons of that category when it changes
#                                  weapon, in percent of normal (100 = normal, 150 = faster); categories:
#                                  melee firearm magic special
#   damage <kind|category> <pct>   damage the class deals (kinds: blade bullet shell belt
#                                  fire tempest spirit hellfire; categories: melee firearm
#                                  magic special).  A kind overrides its category.
#   firerate <category> <pct>      fire rate of that category of weapon
#   spread <category> <pct>        spread of that category of weapon (lower = more accurate)
#
# unlock campaign: the class is hidden in the menu until every non-secret map has been finished
# (any difficulty, single player or co-op; see begotten_profile.txt and the BGPROGRESS lump).
# While the "Unlock All Classes (Dev)" option is on, locked classes are always selectable.
#
# Parry (classes with "parry <tics>"): alt fire with the knife raises a guard.  For <tics> tics
# (swordsman: 10) everything coming from the front is turned aside: projectiles are sent
# where the player aims (at the monster under the crosshair, else straight ahead) at twice
# the speed and twice the damage (bosses' too), bullets hit the shooter instead, and a melee attacker is
# stunned for about a second and shoved back (bosses are shoved but never stunned).  The player is planted while guarding, and the button has to be pressed again for every parry.
# Every parried blow renews the window (a burst of shots is parried shot after shot), shoves the
# player back a little, and spares the recovery; a miss leaves the player open for ~0.5 s.
#
# Class art (everything is optional; whatever a class has no art for uses the stock art):
#   sprite <ORIG> <NEW>            draw this class' things / weapons with sprite NEW wherever the
#                                  stock game uses sprite ORIG.  Player body: "sprite PLAY CPLY";
#                                  pistol in hand: "sprite PISG CPIS" (see the table below).  Put
#                                  the lumps (CPLYA1, CPLYA2A8 ...) between S_START and S_END of
#                                  your WAD, frames A, B, C ... without gaps, as for any sprite.
#                                  A frame the class does not have is drawn with the stock sprite.
#   sound <slot> <lump>            this class' own voice instead of the stock player sounds.  Slots:
#                                    pain    taking damage              (stock DSPLPAIN)
#                                    death   dying                      (stock DSPLDETH)
#                                    xdeath  dying gibbed / by massive damage (stock DSPDIEHI, DSSLOP)
#                                    oof     landing hard / hitting a wall (stock DSOOF)
#                                    noway   pressing use on something that will not open (stock DSNOWAY)
#                                    jump    jumping (no stock sound: silent unless you set one)
#                                  <lump> is the sound lump name, e.g. "sound pain DSWPAIN".  A slot left out
#                                  keeps the stock sound; "sound pain -" puts the stock sound back.
#   pose <kind> <SPRITE|-> [frames [tics]] [weapon <name>]
#                                  how OTHER players (and you, in split-screen / the mirror of the
#                                  network) see this class, in the world.  <SPRITE> is a 4-letter
#                                  sprite name (lumps SPRTA1.. SPRTA8, SPRTB1.. ...); "-" removes the
#                                  pose.  frames = how many frames (A, B, C ...; default 1), tics = game
#                                  tics each frame stays (default 4).  Kinds:
#                                    stand   idle (frames loop)
#                                    run     walking / running (frames loop from the first step)
#                                    shoot   attacking: plays A.. from the moment of the shot, holds the last
#                                            frame (the stock muzzle-flash brightness is kept)
#                                    jump    frame A rising, B at the peak, C falling (also when dropping off
#                                            a ledge); frames/tics are ignored
#                                    parry   while the guard is up (swordsman): plays A.. as the guard clock runs; with three or more frames the last one
#                                            is an outward swing shown for a few tics after a parried blow, the others hold
#                                  With "weapon <name>" (names as in BGWEAPON) the pose is only used while
#                                  that weapon is in hand; a weapon pose wins over the class default.
#                                  Priority: parry, shoot, jump, run, stand.  A kind without a pose falls
#                                  back to the stand pose of that weapon, then to the normal sprite.
#                                  Pain and death keep the normal (class "sprite PLAY ...") frames.
#                                  All 8 directions are drawn as separate pictures when the lumps are
#                                  SPRTA1 SPRTA2 ... SPRTA8 (no mirroring); 16 directions are possible too.
#                                  Frames must not have gaps; a missing frame uses the nearest earlier one.
#   edit <class>                   reopens an existing class (soldier / witch / swordsman) and changes
#                                  only the lines that follow, keeping everything else.  Handy in a
#                                  separate BGCLASS lump that adds poses to the built-in classes.
#   face <XYZ>                     status bar faces: lumps XYZST00 XYZST01 ... instead of STFST00
#                                  STFST01 ... (same names as the stock STF* lumps, with XYZ in
#                                  place of STF); a face missing from the set uses the stock one.
#   aircontrol <pct>               steering while airborne, as a percentage of the ground acceleration (0 = a
#                                  jump only keeps its momentum). Steering never makes you faster than a
#                                  running player, but it keeps any speed you already had (a lunge).
#   charge <tics> <min> <max>      held attack (the knife / sword button held down): <tics> to a full charge,
#                                  and the stab's damage at a split-second hold / at a full charge. A click
#                                  (released within 9 tics) is the normal blade attack ("blade").
#   lunge <min> <max>              how fast the stab propels the player, map units per tic, at the weakest /
#                                  full charge. On a hit the target is pushed with that momentum, and the stab's
#                                  damage scales with the player's speed at impact (full while still carried,
#                                  never below 25%).
#   riposte <damage>               a click on a stunned monster does this instead of a slash.
# Stock sprite names: PLAY (player body); weapons held in the view: PUNG (knife / snap),
# SAWG (chainsaw), PISG (pistols), SHTG (rifle / arc lightning), SHT2 (scattergun),
# CHGG (machinegun / chaingun), MISG (fireball / hellfire), PLSG (tornado / devil's breath),
# BFGG (thunderclap); muzzle flashes PISF SHTF SHT2 CHGF MISF PLSF BFGF.
#
# Class-flagged map things (Hexen thing flags Class 1/2/3 in Ultimate Doom
# Builder) are only spawned for the matching class; a thing with none of the
# three flags is spawned for everybody.

class soldier "Soldier"
  health 100
  armor 0
  speed 90
  jump 28
  aircontrol 15
  maxhealth 100
  maxbonus 200
  maxsoul 200
  megahealth 200
  weapons fist pistol
  ammo bullets 50
  damage firearm 115
  damage magic 85
  firerate firearm 110
  firerate magic 90
  spread firearm 85
  spread magic 115
  swapspeed firearm 150
  swapspeed magic 75

class witch "Witch"
  health 90
  armor 0
  speed 110
  jump 37
  aircontrol 30
  maxhealth 90
  maxbonus 180
  maxsoul 180
  megahealth 180
  weapons fist pistol plasma
  ammo bullets 40
  ammo fire 20
  maxammo tempest 125
  maxammo fire 125
  maxammo spirit 125
  damage firearm 85
  damage magic 125
  firerate firearm 90
  firerate magic 110
  spread firearm 120
  spread magic 85
  swapspeed magic 150
  swapspeed firearm 75

class swordsman "Swordsman"
  health 120
  armor 0
  speed 120
  jump 56
  aircontrol 80
  maxhealth 120
  maxbonus 220
  maxsoul 220
  megahealth 220
  parry 7
  foeaim 0
  unlock campaign
  meleeonly
  blade 45 55
  charge 70 1 100
  lunge 10 24
  riposte 200
  weapons fist
